 the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=7$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=4+8\\text{i},$ respectively. \nGiven that $A=PB{P}^{-1},$ which of the following could be the matrix $P?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071697/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce805066c1aa047de8640e8e15e03d4ab24fb938955a97cd746937fef1b5f487"} {"question" "q-135662" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that if $A$ is a real $3\\times 3$ matrix that has one real eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}$ with corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1},$ and two complex eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{3}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{3},$ then $A=PB{P}^{-1},$ where\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\text{Re}({\\lambda }_{2}) & \\text{Im}({\\lambda }_{2}) \\\\ 0 & -\\text{Im}({\\lambda }_{2}) & \\text{Re}({\\lambda }_{2})\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | \\\\ {v}_{1} & \\text{Re}({v}_{2}) & \\text{Im}({v}_{2}) \\\\ | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSwapping the blocks on the main diagonal of $B$ will result in switching the corresponding columns in $P.$\n\nFrom our block diagonal matrix\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 4\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwe deduce that the first column of $P$ will correspond to the real eigenvector ${v}_{1}$ and the second and third columns of $P$ will correspond to the complex eigenvector ${v}_{2}:$\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071697/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce805066c1aa047de8640e8e15e03d4ab24fb938955a97cd746937fef1b5f487"} {"question" "q-135662" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Co